WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.304
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:07.912 --> 00:00:09.620
ROGER MARTINEZ: More
and more enterprises

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:11.120
are modernizing
their infrastructure

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:12.980
by moving to the cloud
and adopting DevOps

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:15.450
as a way to deliver
better software faster

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:17.722
and more reliably.

00:00:17.722 --> 00:00:20.180
Thanks to our friends on the
DevOps Research and Assessment

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:22.850
Team, we know that, on
average, the best performing

00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:25.460
organizations see a higher
deployment frequency,

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:28.640
have less lead time for changes,
have a lower change failure

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:31.640
rate, and take less
time to restore services

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:33.830
after a failure.

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:36.200
A big part of excelling
at these four key metrics

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.450
is having a robust and
effective continuous delivery

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:39.710
pipeline in place.

00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:41.150
If your software
development team

00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:43.525
is developing and delivering
container-based applications

00:00:43.525 --> 00:00:45.680
on GKE, that can be
challenging, especially when

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:47.780
you've got dozens or even
hundreds of pipelines

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:49.460
across multiple environments.

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:53.450
Introducing Google Cloud Deploy,
a streamlined, fully-managed,

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:56.030
continuous delivery
solution for GKE.

00:00:56.030 --> 00:00:59.490
Google Cloud Deploy addresses
these challenges in three ways.

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:02.660
It's fully managed and scalable,
it has built-in security

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:07.010
controls, and it integrates with
your existing DevOps ecosystem.

00:01:07.010 --> 00:01:08.570
Since it's a
fully-managed service,

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:11.180
that means there's no expensive
infrastructure to setup

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:14.270
or maintain for your GKE
continuous delivery pipeline.

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:17.270
Whether you're a small
startup or a large enterprise,

00:01:17.270 --> 00:01:20.060
Google Cloud Deploy scales your
continuous delivery process

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:22.760
seamlessly and manages
it via simple declarative

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:23.600
configuration.

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:25.610
And however your
operation scales,

00:01:25.610 --> 00:01:28.340
you can have a centralized
view of all of your pipelines,

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:30.980
releases, and deployments
across all of your Google Cloud

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:32.030
projects.

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:34.610
Google Cloud Deploy was designed
with safety and security

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:35.840
in mind.

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:38.090
By leveraging IAM
for easily defined

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:40.010
and granular access
controls, you'll

00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:42.350
be able to designate the
right people to manage release

00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:44.750
promotions, and roll out
and roll back changes

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:47.570
to each environment
with a few quick clicks.

00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:50.390
And Google Cloud Deploy
provides audit logs right out

00:01:50.390 --> 00:01:53.420
of the box, enabling you to meet
your regulatory and compliance

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:55.430
goals as you scale
your release velocity.

00:01:55.430 --> 00:01:57.890
Google Cloud Deploy is designed
to work with your existing

00:01:57.890 --> 00:01:59.630
DevOps ecosystem of products.

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:01.190
Google Cloud Deploy
functionality

00:02:01.190 --> 00:02:03.860
is accessible via
CLI or API, and is

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:05.930
able to integrate with
popular tools you already

00:02:05.930 --> 00:02:07.760
love, like Cloud
Build and Jenkins

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.259
for continuous integration.

00:02:09.259 --> 00:02:12.140
Google Cloud Deploy also brings
scaffold to your pipelines,

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:14.000
improving the
reliability of pipelines

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:16.250
by insulating them from
changes to your tool chain

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:18.200
and application architecture.

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:18.940
Sound good?

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:21.440
You can learn more about Google
Cloud Deploy by checking out

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:22.440
cloud.google.com/deploy.

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:25.090
[MUSIC PLAYING]

